     },
     "caption": "Four ways to look after the environment.",
     "alt": "Four boxes: reduce, reuse, recycle and compost (rot), each with a short meaning."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "What we can do",
     "md": "**Reduce** the waste we make; **reuse** bottles, bags and tins; **recycle** paper, glass, metal and some plastics; **compost** plant waste. **Plant trees** for shade, rain, fuel and homes for animals. Keep **forests and parks** safe because they shelter wildlife such as birds, monkeys and elephants and help to keep rain and soil. Obey rules about hunting and about **protected areas**."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "- Throwing rubbish in drains or rivers.\n- Cutting trees without planting new ones.\n- Thinking that one person's small rubbish does not matter.\n- Burning plastic: the smoke is harmful to people."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1",
     "statement": "Give two ways to reuse an old plastic bottle.",
     "steps": [
      "Think of safe, useful ideas.",
      "Use it as a flower pot or to store dry beans (cleaned first)."
     ],
     "answer": "As a plant pot or for storing dry goods."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 2",
     "statement": "Why is deforestation a problem?",
     "steps": [
      "Trees give shelter to animals, hold the soil and give us rain and shade.",
      "When forests are cut, animals lose homes and soil is washed away."
     ],
     "answer": "Animals lose their homes and soil is eroded."
    }
   ],
